{
  "row": {
    "id": 20,
    "scenario": "Compaction, lead/worker handoff, a cancelled task",
    "required_outcome": "Provenance, trust labels and budgets preserved; failed output never promoted"
  },
  "design": ["§4 Initial limits: 8 KiB combined automatic context, 2 KiB pinned sub-budget, at most 8 retrieved chunks", "§5 steps 2, 7, 8: pinned notes within a sub-budget; every delivery carries id, path, heading, line range, revision, sources, match reason and freshness; delivered as quoted data; `memory_used` reported; the lead's and subagents' deliveries appear in the recently-used ring with their task_id", "§5: the memory section leaves the cached dynamic-context layer (a repeated identical query does not reuse a stale section)", "§6 Promotion and correction: failed or cancelled tasks and assistant-only completion claims never become facts", "§7a per-surface table: lead and subagents read only; task-output extraction yields `extracted_other` candidates only"],
  "loads_in": ["slice-3"],
  "notes_for_implementer": "Twelve notes of about 1.5 KiB on one topic, three of them pinned at about 1 KiB each. Step 1: a recall on that topic returns at most 8 chunks and at most 8192 bytes including the pinned notes and wrappers, with at most 2048 bytes of pinned notes (so two of the three), and reports truncation. Step 2: the lead's delivery carries the full provenance per item and is not a system instruction; step 3 the subagent's narrowed context gets the same items with the same provenance, read-only. Step 4: a service write between two identical recalls is visible in the second (nothing is cached by query text). Steps 5–7: task-output extraction from a cancelled task, a failed task and an assistant-only completion claim never produces an active note — the first two produce nothing, the third at most an `extracted_other` candidate. Step 8: the recently-used ring lists the lead's delivery with its task_id. The 1.5 KiB bodies use the generator so the byte budget is real.",
  "owners": [
    { "id": "u_example_alice", "owner_key": "32acea7eb739b08afd959db91e46d450" }
  ],
